{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Cast</b> — He says to his soul, or to the righteous one: cast your burden upon HaShem." "<b>And He will sustain you</b> — He will bear you, as in: השמים לא יכלכלוך (the heavens will not bear you), and: מי מכלכל את יום בואו (who can bear the day of his coming)." "Some say: the word יהבך — as in 'gave you.' The meaning: the burden that HaShem placed upon you. Rabbi Moses said: 'gave you' — its meaning is 'He will give you bread until now, and He will sustain you in the future,' as in: ויכלכל יוסף (and Joseph sustained). This is not the meaning of the psalm."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 55, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:54.817290121Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}